questions=[
 ('Does a reviewer role alone authorize every case detail request?',['No; the server checks the current actor, action, and record','Yes, if the record ID is hard to guess','Yes, if the UI hides foreign links'],'A role identifies broad capability. The server must still decide whether this actor may perform this action on this current record.'),
 ('When should a protected collection apply authorization?',['Before counting, ranking, and pagination','After building a global cursor and count','Only when the user opens a detail page'],'Filtering after pagination can reveal counts and create sparse pages. The authorized set must drive collection results and metadata.'),
 ('What does a tenant-scoped cache key replace?',['Nothing about server authorization; it only separates cached representations','Every object-level permission check','Authentication for the worker'],'Tenant scope in a cache key prevents collisions, but a protected cache read still needs a verified actor and authorization decision.'),
 ('Where should a queued export obtain its tenant scope?',['From verified server context when the job is accepted','From a client-provided tenantId field','From the artifact filename'],'A privileged worker must not trust a scope selected by the caller. The server creates and validates the job envelope under the current actor.'),
 ('What must happen after a reviewer loses access during an active session?',['Sensitive server requests and live delivery recheck within a defined bound','Only remove the save button after refresh','Allow old signed roles until the user logs out voluntarily'],'Role and assignment changes need server-side enforcement across requests, streams, caches, and delayed artifacts.'),
 ('Is an opaque export artifact ID enough to protect a download?',['No; status and byte delivery each need a scoped grant or current authorization','Yes, if it contains many random characters','Yes, if the first request was authorized'],'An artifact ID may appear in history or logs. Authorization at request, worker, status, and download are separate checks.'),
 ('What belongs in a retention inventory?',['Each active and derived copy with purpose, owner, deadline, and cleanup path','Only the primary database row','Only the browser cookie lifetime'],'Search, exports, media, queues, caches, logs, and backups may each hold copies that need an approved lifecycle.'),
 ('When is an erasure job complete?',['After required active-store outcomes are verified under the policy','Immediately when a queue message is written','When the primary row returns 404'],'Acceptance and primary deletion do not prove that derived copies are gone. Partial failures need a visible repair path.'),
 ('How should a failed search-index deletion appear?',['As a retryable partial failure while protected reads remain gated','As complete because the database row is gone','As a reason to restore the deleted row'],'A derived-store failure is still unfinished work. The record should stay inaccessible and the cleanup owner should be visible.'),
 ('What prevents an old backup from reviving a later-deleted case?',['Replaying durable deletion markers before serving the restored state','Restoring directly into production and trusting the old snapshot','Deleting the marker as soon as the primary row disappears'],'A restore predating deletion can contain the record. Markers and post-restore verification must outlive restorable backups.'),
 ('What should happen to private browser state on account change?',['Clear scoped application-controlled copies and enforce server revocation independently','Keep the old IndexedDB draft visible to the new account','Assume cookie deletion also deletes every cache and downloaded file'],'Memory, persistent storage, and service-worker caches need an identity-transition policy. Server authorization remains the controlling boundary.'),
 ('Can a web app retract an already downloaded export file from a device?',['No; browser cleanup cannot guarantee remote deletion of downloaded files','Yes, by clearing localStorage','Yes, by sending an empty service-worker message'],'A downloaded file has left application-controlled storage. The product should state that limit rather than claiming complete device cleanup.')
]
